cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this project, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Characterising functions for which neural network depth is strictly necessary: a literature review"
abstract: >-
  Literature review written for the introduction to scientific research
  course at Polytech Nice Sophia (MAM3). It surveys the depth separation
  results of neural network theory, from the universality theorems of
  Cybenko and Hornik to the spectral characterisation of Diakonikolas et
  al. and the barriers of Vardi et al., and asks whether the functions that
  need depth admit a mathematical characterisation.
